<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Somaliland</h1><p class="st-meta">1960 CE – 1960 CE · capital Hargeisa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The independent state formed from British Somaliland, which existed for just five days in 1960 before uniting with the south.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-somaliland">British Somaliland</a> received independence on 26 June 1960 as the State of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, with a legislative assembly elected earlier that year and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-haji-ibrahim-egal">Muhammad Haji Ibrahim Egal</a> as prime minister. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland's</a> later governments state that some 35 countries, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a>, recognised it.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>There was no time for a separate state to take shape. Its leaders had already agreed to unite with the south, and the union was rushed through with an act signed hastily and never properly ratified by both sides, a fact later cited by northern separatists.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 1 July 1960 the State of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Somaliland</a> united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-somaliland">Trust Territory of Somaliland</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-republic">Somali Republic</a>. Its short-lived independence is the legal basis claimed by the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, which declared its independence in 1991.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-somaliland.jpg" alt="State of Somaliland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Siirski · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_State_of_Somaliland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1960 CE – 1960 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hargeisa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad Haji Ibrahim Egal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Somaliland (1960)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=state-of-somaliland" aria-label="State of Somaliland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5896 1820 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Somaliland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6216 2076L6240 2044M6216 2076L6259 2357M6216 2076L6216 2076"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6240 2044h0M6259 2357h0M6216 2076h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6216 2076h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6216 2076h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hargeisa. <a href="/atlas?year=1960&amp;focus=state-of-somaliland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
